    {
     "tabId": "29452264-942d-5034-904e-1dfe550dfd28",
     "collapsed": false,
     "id": "ed6f28e0-6ce2-5bfc-ab3d-d5c0dce1480a",
     "gridsterCoords": {
      "w": 12,
      "x": 1,
      "h": 7,
      "y": 54
     },
     "type": "TextDisplay",
     "title": "How to read this",
     "config": {
      "locationUrl": "",
      "locationFile": "",
      "editorData": "<div style=\"font-family:'Metropolis','Segoe UI',sans-serif;font-size:13px;padding:12px 14px;background:#2b3137;color:#e9edf0;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);border-radius:6px\">\n<h2 style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin:2px 0 10px 0;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN network &mdash; how is each layer of the network path behaving?</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN traffic crosses four layers, and each has a panel here from the top down: <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">RDT</b>, vSAN's own transport; <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">TCP</b>; the VMkernel network adapter (<b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vmknic</b>); and the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">physical NIC</b>. Two further panels show every uplink as vCenter counts it, and cluster membership (CMMDS) traffic.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Most columns show the highest value in the selected period, so a short burst inside a five-minute interval is not averaged away. Columns that behave differently, such as minimums, current values and cumulative counts, are described in the reference below.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">High pNIC error rate</b> shows the eight counters behind vCenter's built-in alarm <i style=\"font-style:italic;color:#e9edf0\">High pNic error rate detected</i> (alarm-261): <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">rxCrcErr</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">rxErr</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">rxFifoErr</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">rxMissErr</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">rxOvErr</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">txCarErr</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">txErr</code> and <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">pauseCount</code>, with the cumulative <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">rxMissErrRaw</code>. The alarm is raised when the vSAN health test for any of those counters reports yellow or red. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">pNIC stats - every counter</b> shows the full set of pNIC columns.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">The pNIC panels list the uplinks the vSAN Performance Service reports on. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Every uplink - from vCenter</b> shows all uplinks on each host, counted by vCenter.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Reading any column here</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">A blank cell is not a zero.</b> A blank cell means no value was collected for that column in the selected period.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Raw columns are cumulative counts.</b> Where a column has a Raw twin, the Raw column is the cumulative count and the other column is a per-interval rate.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">RDT latencies - per vmknic</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN vmknic RDT Latency</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Max Out Context Bytes</span> &mdash; Maximum outbound RDT context bytes over the last 5 seconds.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">VNIC Avg Lat</span> &mdash; Average round-trip latency of vSAN's own transport between hosts. This sits above TCP, so it can be slow while every NIC counter is clean.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Cluster Max Lat</span> &mdash; Worst round-trip latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Cluster Min Lat</span> &mdash; Best round-trip latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Avg Out Queueing Lat</span> &mdash; Average time a message waited in the outbound queue before being sent. Queueing, as opposed to time on the wire.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Max Out Queueing Lat</span> &mdash; Worst outbound queueing delay in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Socket Min Out Bytes (Low Is Bad)</span> &mdash; Lowest free space in the outbound socket buffer in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Socket Min In Bytes (Low Is Bad)</span> &mdash; Lowest free space seen in the inbound socket buffer. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Low is bad</b>, for the same reason.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Keepalive reset (Total)</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of RDT keepalive resets.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Num ready delay (Total)</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of ready delays.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">TCP error types</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Host TCP Health</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">TCP TX retransmit (rate)</span> &mdash; Segments this host retransmitted because they were not acknowledged.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">TCP RX errors (rate)</span> &mdash; Inbound TCP segments rejected as erroneous.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Received Duplicate Acknowledge Rate</span> &mdash; Duplicate acknowledgements received by this host.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Received Duplicate Packets Rate</span> &mdash; Duplicate packets received: data that arrived more than once.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Received Out-of-order Packets Rate</span> &mdash; Packets received out of order.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Sack Received Blocks Rate</span> &mdash; SACK (selective acknowledgement) blocks received.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Sack Send Blocks Rate</span> &mdash; SACK (selective acknowledgement) blocks sent.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Sack Rexmits Rate</span> &mdash; Segments retransmitted on the basis of SACK information.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Timeout Drop Rate</span> &mdash; Established connections dropped because the retransmission timer expired.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Half Open Drop Rate</span> &mdash; Half-open drop rate for the VMkernel network adapter.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">TCP Send Zero Window (Total)</span> &mdash; Times this host advertised a zero receive window to a peer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">TCP Errors (Total)</span> &mdash; Total TCP errors recorded by this host's stack since boot.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">vmknic - the kernel port</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN vmknic</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Out Packet Discard Rate</span> &mdash; Proportion of outbound packets discarded at the host network layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">In Packet Discard Rate</span> &mdash; Proportion of inbound packets discarded at the host network layer, across all of this host's vSAN traffic rather than one uplink.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Throughput In</span> &mdash; Inbound throughput for this host's vSAN traffic. Context for the error columns.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Throughput Out</span> &mdash; Outbound throughput for this host's vSAN traffic.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">In Packets Per Second</span> &mdash; Inbound packets per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Out Packets Per Second</span> &mdash; Outbound packets per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Port RX packets</span> &mdash; Packets received on this kernel port.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Port TX packets (Total)</span> &mdash; Packets transmitted on this vSwitch port.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">In Packet Drop Rate (vSwitch port)</span> &mdash; Inbound packets dropped by the vSwitch for this port.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Out Packet Drop Rate (vSwitch port)</span> &mdash; The vSwitch discarded outbound packets for this port.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">High pNIC error rate</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN High pNIC Error Rate</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX CRC Error</span> &mdash; The frame arrived damaged and failed its checksum. One of the eight counters behind vCenter's built-in alarm <i style=\"font-style:italic;color:#e9edf0\">High pNic error rate detected</i> (alarm-261), which is raised when the vSAN health test for any of them reports yellow or red.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX Generic Error</span> &mdash; Receive errors not attributed to a more specific counter. Useful as a catch-all; look to the specific counters first.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX FIFO Error</span> &mdash; The NIC's own on-chip buffer overflowed before it could move packets across PCIe into host memory. The NIC could not hand data over fast enough.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX Missed Error</span> &mdash; The NIC's receive ring had no free descriptor, so the packet was dropped before the driver saw it. Distinct from a drop (discarded higher up) and an error (arrived damaged). This table covers the uplinks the vSAN Performance Service reports on, which are the uplinks carrying vSAN traffic.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX Buffer Overflow Error</span> &mdash; Receive buffer overflow errors on the physical NIC.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC TX Carrier Error</span> &mdash; Carrier lost while transmitting.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC TX Generic Error</span> &mdash; Transmit errors not attributed to a more specific counter.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNic 802.3x Pause Rate</span> &mdash; 802.3x pause frames, the flow control a host and a switch use to ask each other to slow down. The counter has no direction: it does not separate pause frames received from pause frames sent. Pause frames are exchanged only when flow control is enabled on the uplink; an uplink's settings can be listed with <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">esxcli network nic pauseParams list</code>.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX Missed Error (Total)</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of missed receive errors. The column of the same name without Raw is the per-interval rate.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">pNIC stats - every counter</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN pNIC Errors</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX Missed Error</span> &mdash; The NIC's receive ring had no free descriptor, so the packet was dropped before the driver saw it. Distinct from a drop (discarded higher up) and an error (arrived damaged). This table covers the uplinks the vSAN Performance Service reports on, which are the uplinks carrying vSAN traffic.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX CRC Error</span> &mdash; The frame arrived damaged and failed its checksum. One of the eight counters behind vCenter's built-in alarm <i style=\"font-style:italic;color:#e9edf0\">High pNic error rate detected</i> (alarm-261), which is raised when the vSAN health test for any of them reports yellow or red.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX Generic Error</span> &mdash; Receive errors not attributed to a more specific counter. Useful as a catch-all; look to the specific counters first.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX FIFO Error</span> &mdash; The NIC's own on-chip buffer overflowed before it could move packets across PCIe into host memory. The NIC could not hand data over fast enough.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX Buffer Overflow Error</span> &mdash; Receive buffer overflow errors on the physical NIC.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC TX Carrier Error</span> &mdash; Carrier lost while transmitting.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC TX Generic Error</span> &mdash; Transmit errors not attributed to a more specific counter.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">In Packet Drop Rate (pNIC port)</span> &mdash; Inbound packets dropped by the vSwitch for this port.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Out Packet Drop Rate (pNIC port)</span> &mdash; The vSwitch discarded outbound packets for this port.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNic 802.3x Pause Rate</span> &mdash; 802.3x pause frames, the flow control a host and a switch use to ask each other to slow down. The counter has no direction: it does not separate pause frames received from pause frames sent. Pause frames are exchanged only when flow control is enabled on the uplink; an uplink's settings can be listed with <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">esxcli network nic pauseParams list</code>.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">IO chain drops</span> &mdash; Packets dropped in the ESXi IO chain.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">IO chain RX drops</span> &mdash; Inbound packets dropped in the ESXi IO chain.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">IO chain TX drops</span> &mdash; Outbound packets dropped in the ESXi IO chain.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX Missed Error (Total)</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of missed receive errors. The column of the same name without Raw is the per-interval rate.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC RX CRC Error (Total)</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of CRC errors. The column of the same name without Raw is the per-interval rate.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">pNIC PFC Count (Total)</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of priority flow control frames.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Port TX packets (Total)</span> &mdash; Packets transmitted on this vSwitch port.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Every uplink - from vCenter</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Host Uplinks and Load</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Uplink RX Errors, All NICs</span> &mdash; Inbound errors summed across every uplink on the host, counted by vCenter rather than by this pack.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Uplink RX Dropped, All NICs</span> &mdash; Inbound packets dropped across every uplink on the host.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Uplink TX Errors, All NICs</span> &mdash; Outbound errors across every uplink on the host.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Uplink TX Dropped, All NICs</span> &mdash; Outbound packets dropped across every uplink on the host.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Host Network Throughput</span> &mdash; Network throughput of the host, all uplinks and all traffic types, as reported by vCenter.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Host CPU Usage</span> &mdash; CPU usage of the host, as reported by vCenter.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Host CPU Contention</span> &mdash; CPU contention for the host: the proportion of time virtual machines waited for CPU, as reported by vCenter.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Host Memory Consumed</span> &mdash; Proportion of host memory consumed.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Host Memory Swap-In Rate</span> &mdash; Rate at which the host reads swapped memory back from disk, as reported by vCenter.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Host Uptime</span> &mdash; Time since the host last booted.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Hardware Sensor Status</span> &mdash; Overall hardware sensor health, as the host's own sensors report it.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Connectivity Issues, Critical</span> &mdash; Count of critical connectivity findings against this host.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Utilisation Issues, Critical</span> &mdash; Count of critical utilisation findings against this host.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">CMMDS - cluster membership</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN CMMDS Network</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Out</span> &mdash; Cluster directory messages sent by this host. CMMDS is how hosts agree on cluster membership and object placement; if it cannot talk, the cluster partitions, and that happens before any IO metric moves.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read In</span> &mdash; Cluster directory messages received.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Out Throughput</span> &mdash; CMMDS network read outbound throughput, in bytes per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read In Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second of inbound cluster directory traffic.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Group Out Unicast</span> &mdash; Unicast membership messages sent.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Group In</span> &mdash; Membership messages received.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Group Out Unicast Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second of outbound unicast membership traffic.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Group In Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second of inbound membership traffic.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Group Out Multicast</span> &mdash; Multicast membership messages sent.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Group Out Multicast Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second of outbound multicast membership traffic. Expected to be zero.</p>\n</div>\n",
